    <label>Sixth Form: Whirling Peach</label>
    <description>A technique performed during or immediately after an evasive step — the user pivots on their heel, letting the body's full momentum spiral outward into a single sweeping slash. The grace of the movement makes it almost indistinguishable from a dodge until the blade has already passed.</description>
